EXTENSION "ArM5_Hermetic_Projects_GreatTower_Devices" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Hermetic Projects - Chapter Three: The Great Tower devices"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-05"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Hermetic_Projects_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's devices, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t71a77555d51e01197c165d ^"The Arms of Hercules" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Herbam"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 40
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Unlimited Use"
            ^"Range" STRING "Sight"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Concentration"
            ^"Target" STRING "Group"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 4, +3 Sight, +1 Concentration, +1 Group, +1 Size; +10 Unlimited Use)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (80), 2 seasons (60), 3 seasons (54), 4 seasons (50)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReHe 40 Pen: +0, Unlimited Use R: Sight, D: Concentration, T: Group"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 40
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This large crane is used by mundane craftsmen to raise blocks of stone from hundreds of feet below them to where they need it, solving two problems from which its mundane counterparts suffer. First, it can move the stone from any point that the operator can see to any other such place under the operator’s guidance. Second, the crane can effortlessly lift huge weights in a controlled manner where others strain and buckle.\n\nThe Arms of Hercules is a huge wooden structure, requiring 10 pawns of vis to prepare it for enchantment. As a crane, it provides a shape bonus of +5 to effects that lift things. This effect only uses four of the available 10 pawns of space in the device.\n\nThe Group target, combined with an additional magnitude for size, allows the crane to lift 100 cubic paces of stone blocks with each use.\n\nUse of the Arms of Hercules crane adds +1 to the Mason’s Craft: Mason ability for the purposes of determining how long the structure takes to build (*City & Guild*, page 68).\n\nThe crane’s shape bonus provides +5 to the Lab Total."
    }

    #tcf01c1de8a255efb71bc38 ^"True Falsework" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Herbam"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 30
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "24/day"
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Momentary"
            ^"Target" STRING "Group"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 5, +1 Touch, +2 Group, +1 flexibility; +5 24/day)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (60), 2 seasons (45), 3 seasons (40), 4 seasons (38)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReHe 30 Pen: +0, 24/day R: Touch, D: Momentary, T: Group"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 40
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A character using this enchanted leather glove is able to build a discrete section of falsework, scaffolding, shoring, or centering in a moment by touching the glove to a pile of wood and rope. Wooden dowels are formed to pin the joints together, which are strengthened with the rope to provide a stable structure. The falsework can be of any design.\n\nThe standard Rego craft magic Perception + Finesse stress roll is required against a variable Ease Factor:\n\nFalsework Ease Factor Scaffolding 9 Shoring 12 Centering 15\n\nParticularly elaborate falsework may have higher Ease Factors.\n\nHaving one or more characters use the glove for a year adds +1 to the mason’s Craft: Mason score for the purposes of determining how much is achieved during that year.\n\nThe Lab Total benefits from a +4 bonus for affecting things by touch, due to its Shape and Material bonus as the effect is enchanted into a glove."
    }

    #t3ae27647d82e8c7baafb44 ^"The Stonemason’s Art" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Terram"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 15
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Perdo"
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Unlimited use"
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Momentary"
            ^"Target" STRING "Individual"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 2, +1 Touch, +1 stone, +1 flexibility; +10 for unlimited use)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (30), 2 seasons (23), 3 seasons (20), 4 seasons (19)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "Re(Pe)Te 15 Pen: +0, Unlimited use R: Touch, D: Momentary, T: Individual"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 41
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Given a single block of stone, this chisel enchanted with a Rego craft magic effect chips away at the stone under the control of its wielder to create the correctly formed shape, be it part of a column, a ceiling rose, or a fully-formed statue.\n\nA Per + Finesse stress roll is required to control this spell against an Ease Factor that increases with the complexity of the piece.\n\nItem Ease Factor An even stone block 9 A column drum 12 A ceiling vault rib 15\n\nUse of this device adds +1 to the mason’s Craft: Mason when determining how long construction takes.\n\nThe Perdo requisite is required as the spell does not simply process or rearrange components but diminishes the stone, by destroying parts of the block, in order to do its work.\n\nThis device is best designed as a lesser enchantment, as even a small iron tool takes 10 pawns of vis to prepare for enchantment. The shape of the chisel provides a bonus of +4 to shape or destroy stone, which means that the magus only needs a Lab Total of 26 to enchant this effect in a single season. Experimentation may help to reach this, in which case the chisel may produce particularly attractive or unsightly work, or may introduce flaws to the stones that may only be noticed when it is too late."
    }

    #t7f933f149a8265e9ba1911 ^"The Laborer’s Rest" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Terram"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 25
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Unlimited Use"
            ^"Range" STRING "Voice"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Concentration"
            ^"Target" STRING "Individual"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 3, +2 Voice, +1 Concentration, +1 stone; +10 for unlimited use)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (50), 2 seasons (38), 3 seasons (34), 4 seasons (32)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReTe 25 Pen: +0, Unlimited Use R: Voice, D: Concentration, T: Individual"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 41
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This small wooden wand allows the wielder to move blocks of stone with the power of his voice. The blocks are hefted into the air by magical forces, following their master’s commands.\n\nUse of this device adds +1 to the mason’s Craft: Mason when determining how long construction takes.\n\nThe wand provides a +4 bonus to control things at a distance. Experimentation may distort the effect, so that any one stone block can only be targeted once, or the effect might be restricted to certain types of stone."
    }

    #t284798d816c8f550ebe4f4 ^"The Water Wheel" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Herbam"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 44
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Arcane Connection"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Group"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 3, +4 Arcane Connection, +2 Sun, +2 Group, +1 size; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise/set)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (88), 2 seasons (66), 3 seasons (59), 4 seasons (55)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReHe 44 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Arcane Connection, D: Sun, T: Group"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 41
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This water wheel is seeded with arcane connections to other water wheels located elsewhere in the tower. As another water wheel is made, one of the slats of the wheel is processed to make a fixed arcane connection. This arcane connection is then fitted into the central wheel, allowing the device to act over the remote wheel.\n\nAs the main water wheel turns, each other wheel to which it has an arcane connection turns at the same pace, as though it was pushed by the same force of water.\n\nBy tying the action of the targets to the action of this wheel, the base effect is reduced, from moving the target in an unnatural fashion to a natural fashion, because of the action of the water. In this way, the central water wheel powers grain mills, forges, cranes, and other devices.\n\nEach craftsman that can make use of a wheel gains a +1 Innovation bonus to his Workshop Total. This cannot take the workshop’s total innovation bonus beyond +3.\n\nThe shape of the wheel provides a +2 bonus to constant effects."
    }

    #t05318af3e8b57a5808f6ff ^"The Flying Buttress" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Terram"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 29
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Personal"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Individual"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 3, +2 Sun, +1 stone, 3 size; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise/set)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (58), 2 seasons (44), 3 seasons (39), 4 seasons (37)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReTe 29 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Personal, D: Sun, T: Individual"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 41
        }
        DESCRIPTION "One distinctive feature of cathedrals across Mythic Europe is the set of external supports, or buttresses, that help strengthen and support the structure’s walls. These work by distributing the weight, load, and lateral forces placed on the structure by its own mass and, in particular, the roof.\n\nButtresses in mundane buildings need to be anchored firmly into the ground to disperse the forces, but this is impossible with the Great Tower. In this case, the buttresses must support themselves through Rego magic.\n\nThese devices take the form of small pillars external to the Great Tower. They are connected through stonework built out from the tower to the buttress, usually in a sweeping arch, but a straight bridge of stone may be used. Each buttress is enchanted such that the pillar floats in mid-air and resists all attempts to move it from its position. This provides a +1 modifier to stress checks against events that threaten to damage the tower. The Great Tower can benefit from a number of these devices equal to the master mason’s Craft: Mason score.\n\nThe buttress may be used for other purposes, such as a supporting a watchtower, though building any more than a simple room on top of the pillar detracts from its primary purpose and negates the +1 bonus.\n\nThe additional magnitudes for size in the effect design ensure that the buttress resists the weight of the tower bearing down on it.\n\nThe relatively low lab totals required for this device means that it could be enchanted as a lesser device in a single season. The resulting lab text makes subsequent copies easier still."
    }

    #t04f9f6ff1aa59fb233eae7 ^"The Spider’s Gift" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "Wall Crawler"
            ^"Rules Section" STRING "Wall Crawler"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Terram"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 34
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Individual"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 3, +1 Touch, +2 Sun, +2 Metal, +2 Size; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise and sunset)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (68), 2 seasons (51), 3 seasons (46), 4 seasons (43)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReTe 34 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Touch, D: Sun, T: Individual"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 42
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This is the effect that allows the Wall Crawler both to cling to the wall with no danger of falling, and to move itself under direction from the occupants of the carriage trailing behind the great iron spider."
    }

    #t97b72dd617699f59b9dc84 ^"Convening the Council" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "The Distant Council Chamber"
            ^"Rules Section" STRING "The Distant Council Chamber"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Form" STRING "Imaginem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 59
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Intellego"
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Arcane Connection"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Circle"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 5, +4 Arcane Connection, +2 Sun, +2 for moving images, +1 intricacy, +1 Intellego requisite; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise and sunset)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (118), 2 seasons (89), 3 seasons (79), 4 seasons (74)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "Cr(In)Im 59 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Arcane Connection, D: Sun, T: Circle"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 43
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Projects the image, affecting of all the senses, of everything in this circle into another circle to which it has an arcane connection. The Intellego requisite also shows the contents of the remote circle, linked through the arcane connection present in the device, including all magically created species. It operates over all five senses, so that the magus in his own circle can see, hear, touch, smell, and taste everything that is projected into the distant council chamber.\n\nNote, the species given off by the magus in the circle are not encumbered or inhibited by his Parma Magica and can therefore be sent from the local circle to the remote target. This is essentially an application of the common Haunt of the Living Ghost spell (**ArM5**, page 144) in device form."
    }

    #ted710f819fdc3ebdbef716 ^"The Stone Watchman" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "Gargoyles and Grotesques"
            ^"Rules Section" STRING "Gargoyles and Grotesques"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Intellego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Imaginem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 40
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+42"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Personal"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Vision"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 1, +2 Sun, +4 Vision; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise and sunset, +21 Penetration of 42)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (80), 2 seasons (60), 3 seasons (54), 4 seasons (50)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "InIm 40 Pen: +42, Constant Effect R: Personal, D: Sun, T: Vision"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 44
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This effect gives an enchanted device the power of sight. The grotesque is carved such that it has discernible eyes and this effect gives it a field of vision similar to that possessed by a human. As this is magical vision, the effect does need to penetrate the Magic Resistance of anything within the item’s field of vision (ArM5, page 114). Entities that resist this effect are not “seen” and do not trigger any effects linked to this. Giving the effect a higher Penetration increases the effect’s overall level."
    }

    #td8aac8d713967a2c522a52 ^"Projecting the Watchman’s Gaze" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "Gargoyles and Grotesques"
            ^"Rules Section" STRING "Gargoyles and Grotesques"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Form" STRING "Imaginem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 19
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Arcane Connection"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Individual"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 1, +4 Arcane Connection, +2 Sun; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered by sunrise/set)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (38), 2 seasons (29), 3 seasons (26), 4 seasons (24)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "CrIm 19 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Arcane Connection, D: Sun, T: Individual"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 44
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The images detected through the power of sight granted by the previous effect are projected onto the mirror associated with the bronze shard held by the grotesque. The mirror shows exactly what the grotesque “sees” at that moment and the image fills the mirror’s surface. There is no restriction on the size of the mirror, and the larger it is, the more detail it displays.\n\nGiven the weakness of the stone watchman’s vision, potential threats with strong magical resistance will not be relayed to the mirror. But the nature of the magical vision means that a silhouette within the image *will* be apparent, allowing an astute observer to make assumptions about what happens to be there."
    }

    #t43278f331d1b3e90367fd0 ^"The Restless Watchman" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "Gargoyles and Grotesques"
            ^"Rules Section" STRING "Gargoyles and Grotesques"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Terram"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 24
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Muto"
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Personal"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Individual"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 3, +2 Sun, +1 Muto requisite, +1 affect stone, +1 precise control; +1 for 2/ day, +3 triggered by sunrise/set)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (48), 2 seasons (36), 3 seasons (32), 4 seasons (30)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "Re(Mu)Te 24 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Personal, D: Sun, T: Individual"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 44
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Grotesques are designed to scare away evil spirits and often take the form of winged demonic beasts themselves. This enchantment increases the fearsome effect by giving the stone figure constant motion. The grotesque shifts on its perch, flexes its wings, peers around with its beady eyes, and snatches at imaginary insects with its stone claws.\n\nThis has two side effects. The first is that it increases the grotesque’s field of vision, increasing the area of sky it observes. The second is that regardless of whether any evil spirits are fooled by the statue, mundane birds will rarely roost anywhere near the constantly moving stone beast.\n\nThis effect could easily be enchanted into a separate stone grotesque as a Lesser Enchanted Item."
    }

    #tc11954eee67908937e1b77 ^"Capture the Wind" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Auram"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 34
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Group"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 5, +1 Touch, +2 Sun, +2 Group; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise/set)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (68), 2 seasons (51), 3 seasons (46), 4 seasons (43)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReAu 34 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Touch, D: Sun, T: Group"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 45
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Enchanted into the arms of a windmill, this effect calms and channels the winds associated with even the strongest storms. This is essential for protecting the Great Tower from powerful winds that could cause the tower to shift and sway.\n\nThe base fifth magnitude design controls severe weather phenomena, and the Group target allows it to control and channel 10 individual storm winds. These winds flow around the tower, causing no harm. But sustained storms, either natural or magical, can overwhelm these devices. And of course, these devices have no Penetration, so elemental winds are unaffected.\n\nIf using the rules for damaging objects presented in *City & Guild* each of these devices provides a +1 modifier to stress checks caused by storms (page 77).\n\nDefects introduced through experimentation may cause the device to fail in certain weather, such as rain or snow, or it may give the effect a Penetration score, which may allow it to capture a small spirit of the air that the magi might need to release."
    }

    #t979232abb2ed1e8fdbcb6f ^"The Waterfall" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Aquam"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 59
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Arcane Connection"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Part"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 10, +4 Arcane Connection, +2 Sun, +1 Part, +2 size; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered by sunrise/set)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (118), 2 seasons (89), 3 seasons (79), 4 seasons (74)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReAq 59 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Arcane Connection, D: Sun, T: Part"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 45
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Deep underground, amid the foundations of the tower, several great cisterns collect and store the water that runs in from a nearby stream. This device, in the form of constantly turning waterwheel, magically draws water through a channel up into the tower and over the wheel, where it then cascades back down again.\n\nWater can be collected and channeled from both the ascending stream and the waterfall. The constant flow of water helps to freshen the environment, and chambers can be built within the tower to collect the water, allowing small ponds and streams to form.\n\nThe wheel’s rotation can be stopped, which suspends the effect. This is done so that the wheel can be raised to a new higher position within the tower. This is likely to become an event of some significance, representing as it does not just the passing of time, but also the growth of the tower.\n\nThe wheel provides +2 bonus for a constant effect."
    }

    #tc9c1caeb58ec4e9e2d98d2 ^"The Endless Well" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Aquam"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 65
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "24/day"
            ^"Range" STRING "Arcane Connection"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Momentary"
            ^"Target" STRING "Individual"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 40, +4 Arcane Connection; +5 for 24/day)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (130), 2 seasons (98), 3 seasons (87), 4 seasons (82)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReAq 65 Pen: +0, 24/day R: Arcane Connection, D: Momentary, T: Individual"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 45
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This enchanted bucket draws water from a remote well, by instantly transporting it into the bucket as it is tipped up. Given the height of the tower, it may not be feasible for covenfolk to fetch and carry water between levels, so these buckets replace the need for wells. Such a device may also be useful aboard a ship, where it can reduce the need to carry fresh water, or to those crossing the desert.\n\nThis device is first prepared by having an arcane connection to a spring, well, or other body of water fixed into a bucket. A season is spent preparing the bucket in water collected from the well and a pawn of Vim vis. The magus must attend to the activity throughout the season, at the end of which the bucket has become a permanent connection to the well.\n\nIt is then opened for enchantment with 10 pawns of vis (base 5 for iron, x2 for medium size) during a second season, and the effect can be enchanted from the third season. Although primarily of wood, the bucket is strengthened with iron straps. It is opened as a compound device, with the iron straps the most expensive part to open.\n\nA base effect level of 40 has been used for this device. The starting point for this is the base effect for “Control liquid in an extremely violent way,” as per **ArM5**, page 124, which is then modified based on the difficulty of transporting a Corpus target over a range of distances. Applying one magnitude for transport over five paces, two magnitudes for transport over 50 paces, etc. By following the progression under the Rego Corpus guidelines, we arrive at a base effect level of 40 allowing the effect to transport water to a location defined by an arcane connection.\n\nAs a bucket, the device provides a +5 bonus to transporting water.\n\nOf course, there are alternatives to enchanted buckets or unnatural waterfalls.\n\nDevices could be enchanted that transported water less frequently but in greater quantity, in order to refresh cisterns built at intervals as the tower rises."
    }

    #t1aad75814a60d4e569cf9d ^"Gardens and Orchards" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Form" STRING "Herbam"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 19
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Room"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 1, +1 Touch, +2 Sun, +2 Room, +1 size; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise/set)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (38), 2 seasons (29), 3 seasons (26), 4 seasons (24)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "CrHe 19 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Touch, D: Sun, T: Room"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 46
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A number of large halls within the tower serve as gardens, fields, and orchards. This effect, enchanted using the Traveling Laboratory described earlier, ensures that the plants grow well throughout the year. The plants still need soil, sunlight, and rain, and this spell has little effect if the plants do not have at least these essentials. But gargoyles can collect rain as it falls and route it to these indoor gardens, and simple magic or large open arcades can provide all the sunlight that the growing plants need.\n\nAs the gardens and orchards are subject to constant magical effects, warping will accumulate at the rate of one Warping Point per year. This means that trees and other plants that remain within the orchards will eventually show signs of warping. This may manifest either as flawed crops, reduced yield, or even a slowlygrowing sentience.\n\nThe Traveling Laboratory provides +4 to the lab total."
    }

    #tf2cb742aa16bc681dd1c08 ^"Summoning the Distant Senses" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "Window on the World"
            ^"Rules Section" STRING "Window on the World"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Intellego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Imaginem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 54
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Arcane Connection"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Special"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 5, +4 Arcane Connection, +2 Sun, +3 Special based on Room + 1 magnitude; +1 for 2/day, +3 triggered at sunrise and sunset)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (108), 2 seasons (81), 3 seasons (72), 4 seasons (68)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "InIm 54 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Arcane Connection, D: Sun, T: Special"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 46
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This effect uses all senses at Arcane Connection range, whether that connection is to a person or a place. All of these senses are gathered from the target area of approximately the same size as the room in which the device is housed. This is accommodated by the Special target, based on Room +1 magnitude. The effect has no particular point of view or field of vision, and species for all senses are gathered equally.\n\nIf the target is mobile, then the effect follows the target and the scope of the collected images change as the target moves.\n\nThe information gathered is directly accessible to the device’s user, but the additional effect described next ensures that all present in the room can also see the remote images."
    }

    #t6110c6b2a9fae8dd942e8e ^"Sight of Distant Places" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "Window on the World"
            ^"Rules Section" STRING "Window on the World"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Form" STRING "Imaginem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 44
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Constant Effect"
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Room"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 5, +1 Touch, +2 Sun, +2 Room, +2 moving and complex images; +1 for 2/ day, +3 triggered at sunrise and sunset)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (88), 2 seasons (66), 3 seasons (59), 4 seasons (55)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "CrIm 44 Pen: +0, Constant Effect R: Touch, D: Sun, T: Room"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 46
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This effect displays the images gained by the initial Intellego Imaginem effect. The illusion fills the room connected to the window. All of the information gathered by the first effect is reproduced and the user is able to move through the image by walking and turning within the room.\n\nThe purpose of this effect is to display the Imaginem information gathered by the first effect. Without this second effect, the images (and sounds, tastes, smells, sensations) are accessible only to the device user, identified as the person who triggered the device by inserting the arcane connection into the receptacle. A variant device could be created that omitted this effect, which would limit the experience to a single user at a time."
    }

    #tf8668a7b294fd17ee95e31 ^"The Wizard’s Touch" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "Window on the World"
            ^"Rules Section" STRING "Window on the World"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Terram"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 55
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Animal, Aquam, Corpus, Ignem, Herbam"
            ^"Penetration" STRING "+0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "Unlimited Use"
            ^"Range" STRING "Arcane Connection"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Concentration"
            ^"Target" STRING "Special"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 3, +4 Arcane Connection, +1 Concentration, +3 Special based on Room +1, +2 affect metal and gemstones; +10 Unlimited Use)"
            ^"Required Lab Total" STRING "Required Lab Total: 1 season (110), 2 seasons (83), 3 seasons (74), 4 seasons (69)"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "ReTe (AnAqCoIgHe) 55 Pen: +0, Unlimited Use R: Arcane Connection, D: Concentration, T: Special"
            ^"Source" STRING "Hermetic Projects"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 46
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Through this effect, the magus may manipulate any chosen item within the room or space to which the device has an active arcane connection. In fact, it is more proper to say that the magus may manipulate the room and its contents, but the illusory view of the place allows the magus a degree of control fine enough to identify and affect individual items.\n\nThe prior effects enchanted into this device give him the sensory information he needs to be able to lift, turn, inspect, and move objects of size, up to the standard individual of its type. Typically this effect is activated by the magus physically interacting with the illusion of the objects cast around him in his own room. But there are limits to what the magus can do. As the spell has no Perdo requisite, the magus cannot destroy items (for instance, by crushing the illusions in his hands), but he could lift the item into the air and drop it, or throw it against a wall, perhaps causing it to smash.\n\nThe effect design has a base Rego Terram level of 3 to control or move dirt in a very unnatural fashion, which allows for fine manual control by the device’s user. It also has two additional magnitudes allowing stone, glass, metal, and gemstones to be affected. The requisites listed are free, and simply allow the device to affect nonliving objects made of materials covered by those requisites.\n\nNote an Arcane Connection range, not Sight, is required in order to allow the user to manipulate these remote objects. As discussed in *Magi of Hermes*, the species displayed by the device are not sufficient to form a sight-based link between the magus and his target (page 101)."
    }

}
